{
  "id": "site.holy_spirit",
  "name": "Holy Spirit church and almshouse",
  "name_1343": "Heiliggeist: parish church and almshouse (Pühavaimu)",
  "confidence": "attested institution (priest 1316/1319, almshouse 1334); footprint after the surviving church (OSM); 1343 state per dossier and the maintainer's period rule",
  "sources": [
    "history/dossiers/religion/churches-and-religious-houses.md",
    "history/dossiers/topography/raekoja-plats-extents-1343.md"
  ],
  "period_notes": [
    "Rule (maintainer 2026-10-07): features dated after 1343 are left out; where the 1343 state is unrecorded, a slightly simplified form of the later, documented church is used (plausible composite).",
    "Excluded as dated later: rib vaults, the large Gothic windows and the stone tower (all 1360s), the north portal (1597), the clock (Ackermann, 1684), the painted galleries (17th c.), Notke's altarpiece (1483), the baroque spire.",
    "Attested for 1343: two-aisle hall (north aisle with the choir on its axis, south aisle added by the early 14th century), flat timber ceiling before the vaults, rectangular choir narrower and lower than the nave, crow-stepped gables, almshouse documented 1334.",
    "Unrecorded in 1343, simplified later form: white lime render; square piers with pointed arches between the aisles; two-light lancets with simple tracery and leaded stained glass (smaller than the 1360 windows); a pointed north portal near the west end; plank floor in the nave; plain oak benches; candle crowns; a plain pulpit; a painted winged retable; saint figures on consoles; the bells in a timber turret on the west gable (before the 1360 tower).",
    "Almshouse placed in the angle east of the south aisle beside the choir (layout plausible composite)."
  ],
